Use self.retry(exc=exc) inside a task bound with bind=True to re-execute the task on recoverable errors. The retry call raises a Retry exception, so code after it is not reached unless throw=False. The exc argument passes exception info used in logs and task results.

```python
@app.task(bind=True)
def send_twitter_status(self, oauth, tweet):
    try:
        twitter = Twitter(oauth)
        twitter.update_status(tweet)
    except (Twitter.FailWhaleError, Twitter.LoginError) as exc:
        raise self.retry(exc=exc)
```

Use autoretry_for=(Exception,) to automatically retry the task on any error. The task body is a placeholder with an ellipsis.

```python
@app.task(autoretry_for=(Exception,))
def x():
    ...
```
